      },
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(A)&=P(A\\cap B)+P(A\\cap\\overline{B})\\\\P(A)&=0.1+0.4\\\\P(A)&=0.5.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $A$ and $B$ are independent,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(B)&=\\frac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(A)}\\\\P(B)&=\\frac{0.1}{0.5}\\\\P(B)&=0.2\\\\P(\\overline{B})&=1-0.2\\\\P(\\overline{B})&=0.8\\\\P(A\\cup\\overline{B})&=P(A)+P(\\overline{B})-P(A\\cap\\overline{B})\\\\P(A\\cup\\overline{B})&=0.5+0.8-0.4\\\\P(A\\cup\\overline{B})&=0.9.\\end{align*}$$",
